- Plain pointers for pass-through arguments on the C++ backend (T6).  A step
  built a Variable for every argument it read: the slot, the path from the
  redex, and the set guards crossed; after T5 the hottest instructions of
  the two steps of Tak1 stored those objects on the stack.  An argument that
  the step only passes on to another call needs none of that: nothing
  head-normalizes it from the step (the path), and the value it denotes is
  the node in its slot (the guards).  Done: the generator reads such an
  argument as a plain Node * (the rule is in backends/cxx/passthrough.py).
  A variable is plain when it is declared by IVarDecl, assigned once from a
  successor of the redex or of another variable with a path of one entry,
  from a node the step builds, or from another plain variable, and every use
  passes the value on: an argument of a call, of a partial application, or
  of a choice, the expression of a return (forward_or_copy), or the right
  side of the patch of a recursive let.  A variable that a case scrutinizes
  keeps the Variable (hnf needs the path for the scan and the guards for the
  escape set of a pull-tabbed choice); so do the base of a path and the base
  of a node assignment; the two variables of a var-to-var assignment have
  one kind.  The reads: Node::successor_node(i) (graph/node.hxx) gives the
  node in slot i of the redex, skips a forward node there and shortens the
  slot as the indexer does, and keeps a set guard in the slot, because the
  redex is a function node, never a guard, so the slot holds the whole
  guarded argument (the rvalue of a Variable built the guard again, one node
  per use).  A successor of a Variable (a pattern variable) may lie under
  the guards the Variable crossed, which the ICurry does not show, so
  Variable::successor_node(pos) (graph/indexing.hxx) decides at run time:
  the plain read when the Variable crossed no guard and its target is a
  constructor, the indexer and rvalue otherwise.  A path of more than one
  entry keeps the indexer.  A plain variable starts null (Node * _3 =
  nullptr), as an unassigned Variable yields null: a recursive let builds a
  forward reference from a variable not yet assigned (cyc in
  CxxPassThrough.curry: _2 = Cons n _3 before _3 is assigned, then
  _2.set_successor(1, _3)).  FORMAT_VERSION 6 -> 7.  Static evidence: the
  step of tak in Tak1.so and fibgen in Fib.so call node_reserve,
  node_commit, and compress_fwd_chain only; no smallvec_free, no Variable
  destructor, no guarded_rvalue (objdump).  Measured with the harness (C++
  backend, three repetitions, CPU seconds, before to after, ratio; steps,
