- Y4, goals: defaulting with the PAKCS table and native dictionaries
  (issue #53, fixes #39; #35 in its refuse-to-save form).  A goal without
  a signature is a function whose leading parameters are class
  dictionaries, so curry.eval(M.main14) with main14 = Just 5 came back as
  a partial application.  Done: curry.typecheck.defaulting applies the
  table of the PAKCS REPL (c2p.pl defaultQualType) to a scheme: Num and
  Integral to Int, Fractional and Floating to Float, Monad and MonadFail to
  IO; Data, Eq, Ord, Read and Show dropped on Int and Float, Enum on Int,
  Monad on IO; a lone Data to Bool; anything else the oracle's sentence
  "Cannot handle arbitrary overloaded top-level expressions" with the
  inferred type and a hint.  Apply (T ..) a is folded up to the declared
  arity of T, so return 5 is IO Int.  curry.typecheck.goals applies the
  goal to one base instance per constraint, in the order of the scheme,
  each the partial application of _inst#Class#Type to no argument
  (interp.expr of the symbol); value parameters left over give a function
  value; an IO goal runs during eval and make_value unwraps it (both
  backends did that already).  One path: goals.make_goal in
  Interpreter.eval (a lone function symbol with dictionary parameters),
  compile(mode='expr') without exprtype (the arity check counts the value
  parameters of the scheme; a text that cannot be defaulted is a
