  unit_loadsave.py saves with module_main=False.  Left: curry.expr(M.main14)
  alone still builds the partial application (the typed builder of Y7
  takes it); pure (1, 'a') is an Applicative constraint, which the oracle
  rejects too, so the design's IO unit case is an error case; a lambda
  text goal (\x -> x) fails on the Python backend before this item: the
  expression module is compiled eagerly and importSymbol resolves the
  lifted lambda before loadSymbols loads it (expected failure in
  unit_goals.py); str() of a function value whose head lives in an
  expression module fails in the same way after the module leaves the
