  none), so two children whose modules import a module without them write
  them at once.  The man page names the exception and --jobs 1 for the
  front-end step of such a tree; the comment of curry/Makefile says why
  the prebuild is safe: its ICurry is committed, so the children of the
  C++ step never run the front end.  (3) perf_status read an exit status
  of 255 as 'killed by signal 127'; now only a status that names a signal
  of the machine (signal.valid_signals) reads as one, and 255 stays 255,
