2026-10-06: example 24 rewritten, the rules in the head (worktree wt/ex24c)
- The shape.  The makefile of examples/24-build-system is a plain Curry
  module without imports or type signatures.  The variables are
  definitions with the uppercase names of make (CC = "cc", DEBUG = "0",
  CFLAGS = if DEBUG == "1" then ... else ...), which the pinned front end
  accepts.  A rule is an equation of the relation rule target inputs =
  recipe, with the inputs in the head: the pattern rule is the non-linear
  functional pattern rule (stem ++ ".o") [stem ++ ".c"] = "...", a
  conditional rule is a guard, rule "libgeom.a" ["plot.o"] | WITH_PLOT /=
  "" = "", and the header edges are the relation depends, one equation
  per edge.  The library asks the relation with the inputs free,
  candidate rule t = (ins, rule t ins) where ins free, through set2, and
  both backends bind the inputs (the fix of #98 on this branch).  The
  interpolator of Make.curry expands $@, $<, $^ and $(NAME) from the
  table the driver passes; $(NAME) is strict, anyOf over the entries of
  the name, so a name with two entries is two recipes and a name without
  one is no recipe.  The lints: ambiguous, missing, and the recipes of
  each target (two values or none, with Make.undefined naming the
  variables without a value).  Make.noDepends serves a makefile without
  the relation; Prelude.failed in its place fails the whole build.  The
  include scanner of the driver is gone.  The driver substitutes every
  NAME=value of its command line into the text of the makefile (the
  first line that starts with NAME and = is replaced, other such lines
  are dropped, a missing one is appended), writes the text under
  .curry/overrides/<sha1 of the text> beside the real makefile, puts
  that directory first on curry.path and imports the module from there;
  a second run with the same assignments finds the products (import
  1.06 s cold, 0.17 s warm in the probe).  The variables are read by
  introspection: dir(module), curry.typeof(symbol) in ('String',
  '[Char]'), every value of curry.eval(symbol, converter='topython');
  dir lists the module's own symbols only, so the variant makefiles are
  full copies with one change each (an import-based variant would hide
  its variables from the introspection).  The table goes to Make.build
  and into the environment of every recipe.  Each recipe is printed when
  it starts, as make prints it; the status table, the stand-in for a
  missing compiler and --serve are gone; -j defaults to 1, as in make.
- The toy.  C only: main.c, vec.c, shape.c, report.c (the report.cpp of
  the design prototype turned into C), the optional plot.c, vec.h and
  shape.h.  main.c includes shape.h and vec.h, plot.c includes shape.h,
  so every edge of depends is a real include (cc -MM agrees).  WITH_PLOT=1
  adds plot.o to the library and -DWITH_PLOT to CPPFLAGS, and the program
  prints plot: (0,0) (4,0) (0,3) as its third line.
- The oracle.  GNU make 4.3, make -rn in a clean environment (env -i) on
  a Makefile of the same rules in the scratch directory:
  identical lines in the default world (6, the double space of the empty
  $(CPPFLAGS) included), with DEBUG=1, with WITH_PLOT=1 (7, ar rcs
  libgeom.a vec.o shape.o plot.o: the library puts the inputs of the rule
  with the recipe before the prerequisite lines for this), and after
  touch shape.h (4).  Make's behaviour on the lint cases, for the README:
  two explicit recipes, "warning: overriding recipe for target" and the
  last wins; an explicit rule beside the pattern rule wins in silence;
  CFLAGS assigned twice, the last in silence; $(LDFLAG) undefined,
  nothing in silence; a missing vec.c without a prerequisite line for
  vec.o, "No rule to make target 'vec.o', needed by 'libgeom.a'.  Stop.";
  with the line vec.o: vec.h make counts vec.o as made and prints the ar
  line; the cycle, "Circular shape.h <- demo dependency dropped." and the
  build goes on.
- The run.  Ten steps, eleven make.py processes and two runs of demo:
  the build from scratch with the program's output, nothing to do, touch
  shape.h with --affected and the rebuild, DEBUG=1 -n in a fresh copy,
  WITH_PLOT=1 built in a fresh copy with the third line, the ambiguity
  lint (Makefile_ambiguous.curry), the recipe lint (Makefile_twice.curry,
  CFLAGS twice), the toolchain (Makefile_toolchain.curry, CC = "gcc" ?
  "clang": the recipe lint on five targets, then CC=clang -n in a fresh
  copy), the cycle (Makefile_cycle.curry -n), the missing source.
  Makefile_choice.curry is gone.  The undefined $(NAME) case has no step;
  checked by hand on both backends in a scratch copy: "no recipe for
  demo: $(LDFLAG) is undefined", exit 2.  Also by hand: a makefile
  without depends plans with Make.noDepends; CC=false gives "failed:
  main.o report.o shape.o vec.o" and exit 2; -j 4 prints the recipes in
  the same order as -j 1 (the trace shows the ready sets).
- Times and tests.  ./run on the C++ backend: 10.3 s cold (the library,
  five makefiles and three substituted copies converted), 4.8 s and 6.9 s
  warm; on the Python backend 19.4 s cold, 15.5 s and 16.8 s warm; the
  output identical on both backends, expected.out regenerated.
  tests/unit_examples.py: C++ backend 21 tests OK in 37 s (24-build-system
  6.1 s), Python backend 21 tests OK in 99 s (16.0 s).  A second run of
  the file after the README and driver edits: 21 OK on both backends,
  28.7 s and 127 s.  The direct runs after the last line wraps matched
  expected.out on both backends, 6.1 s and 18.4 s.  The other lane
  shared the machine.
- Review pass, the same day.  Applied: the output of a recipe is shown
  when it completes, stdout to stdout and stderr to stderr (before, the
  driver captured both and showed stderr on failure only, as the driver
  before the rewrite did, so a warning of cc on a compile that succeeded
  was lost); a program that cannot start is a failed recipe with the
  status 127 and the error of the system on stderr, not a traceback from
  the thread pool; $< expands to nothing on a rule without inputs, as in
  make (before, head [] left the recipe without a value and the lint
