  Primes 47 to 9.  CPU seconds, indicative, at a load average twice the
  baseline's: Queens10 1.47 to 0.84 s, Primes 1.74 to 0.70 s.  Fib's
  instructions rise 3.6 percent on equal steps: fibgen adds through a
  dictionary parameter, and isFib never forces the sum, so the selector
  + d (one node) inlined to +._#lambda (apply d ()) (three nodes) costs
  two nodes per element and saves no step; a refinement that inlines a
  body larger than the call only when the rewrite makes progress would
  spare Fib and keep the chains, at the price of the budget rule as the
  plan states it (four 10 with four x = (x + 1, 2) would stay a call); the
  owner decides.  Gate O after O2 and O3: steps Queens10 at most 0.5x
