2026-10-07: the bug batch, #99 and #96, and the lint lines of example 24 (worktree wt/bugs)
- #99, a FlatCurry file written again beside an up-to-date .icy.  The
  writer, found with a probe of the front end (A imports B imports C, B
  with a required equality): a run of the front end on a module compiles
  an import again when the interface (.icurry) of the import is older
  than the interface of one of its own imports, or than its source, or
  when its files are missing; a touch of C.icurry alone does it, a touch
  of C.fint does not.  The run writes the .fcy, .fint and .icurry of the
  import in the text of the front end; the ICurry of the import is
  current by the rule of the toolchain (its source did not change), so
  nothing translates it again; and the route rewrote the file of the
  named module alone.  The main tree shows the mechanism: the install's
  Prelude.icurry was written by a make stage at 10:20 on 2026-10-06,
  CxxInterp.fint and .icurry at 15:26 (a run of the front end on a module
  that imports CxxInterp; unit_cxx_interp.py compiles one from text), the
  .icy of 2026-10-05 untouched, and the hand rewrite of 16:28 changed the
  .fcy alone.  So a make stage that writes the interfaces of the library
  anew makes every module of a tree such an import at its next contact.
  A second writer, outside the toolchain: the PAKCS oracle.  :load M runs
  the front end, which compiles the stale modules of the chain, and :eval
  runs it once more, for the goal, with --acy --flat (parseProgram and
  writeAndParseExpression of c2p.pl), which compiles every module without
  an .acy file again, after BindingOpt rewrote the modules it compiled to
  Prolog: in the probe B.fcy was the text of the front end, without
  constrEq, after :load A :eval main.  No .acy file is under tests/data
  in this worktree or in the main tree, so the oracle wrote no pool
  module there of late.
  The fix.  _frontend.curry2flat takes the stamps (size, time) of the
  .fcy files under .curry/<subdir>/ of every search directory but the
  system library before the run (42 files in the pool, 22 in the library)
  and rewrites every file that is new or changed after it: the module's
  and those of the imports the run compiled again.  A file of an import
  that cannot be read is reported through the log and left; the module's
  own file raises as before.  rewrite=False gives the text of the front
  end to the tests that need it (fresh_flatcurry of
  unit_flat2icurry_bindingopt.py, two tests of unit_curry2icurry.py).
  Both routes go through it; the icurry branch of the converter lost its
  own call of optimize_flatcurry.  The on-disk check:
  flat2icurry_oracle.check_file takes accept_unrewritten; a pair that
  differs is tried once more with the pass over the program in memory,
  and when the pass changes the program and the optimized program
  translates to the .icy, the result is EQUAL with the mark unrewritten
  and a detail.  test_products_on_disk of func_flat2icurry.py passes it,
  names the PAKCS oracle in its docstring as the writer, and prints the
  files that needed it (none in this worktree); the archive is checked
  without it.  Tests: test_import_compiled_again_is_rewritten of
  unit_curry2icurry.py (the A/B/C scenario through the route: the file of
  B keeps constrEq and pairs with its .icy; with rewrite=False the pair
  differs; flatcurry_dirs leaves the system library out), and
  TestUnrewrittenFile of func_flat2icurry.py (the pair of a foreign
  writer, made with the front end alone: DIFFERENT without the keyword,
  EQUAL and marked with it, the file untouched, a real difference stays
  one).  The two usability points: sprite-make --rewrite-flat implies
  --icy and stands alone (the sentence of AGENTS.md holds now; the man
  text and the help say so); run_tests --changed maps
  tests/data/curry/M.curry to the test files whose text names M as a
  word (selection.files_naming; NAMED in RULES), and to everything when
  none does, with the note "no test file names the module M; selects
  everything" (unit_runner.py tests both); on this tree the other lane's
  SetFunctionsBindings.curry maps to unit_setfunctions_bindings.py alone.
