- Boost dropped from the C++ runtime.  Five uses, each replaced by the
  standard library or a few lines: boost::static_log2 by a constexpr
  function (fingerprint.hpp); boost::int_t<N>::exact by the trait
  fingerprints::exact_int<N> over <cstdint> (the same type, int32_t, so
  the layout of Block and the static_assert of Node are unchanged);
  boost::pool<> by fingerprints::BranchPool, a free list over blocks of
  chunks of one size that doubles the block at each refill, as
  boost::pool did (std::pmr::unsynchronized_pool_resource would serve,
  but it finds the pool by size and the chunk by bitmap on every call,
  and the branches are allocated at every copy-on-write of a shared
  fingerprint, so the local pool keeps the O(1) push and pop; it uses the
  throwing ::operator new, where boost::pool returned null); the
  boost::noncopyable base of Configuration, Queue, InterpreterState, Set
  and RuntimeState by deleted copy members (RuntimeState already had
  them; an empty base occupies no storage under the Itanium ABI, so no
  layout changes); and BOOST_PP_CAT, BOOST_PP_STRINGIZE and
  BOOST_PP_TUPLE_ELEM in currylib/defs/not_used.def and unboxed.def by
  local macros with the one indirection each needs (APPLY expands the
  tuple before the element macro sees it; the preprocessed names, the
  strings and sizeof(Node2) are the ones Boost.PP produced).  Gone with
  it: the Boost check of configure (it looked under /usr/include and
  /usr/local/include and wrote nothing into Make.config), the flag
  -I$(BOOST_HOME)/include of Make.include (BOOST_HOME was never defined,
  so the flag was -I/include), the commented Boost blocks of
  Make.validate, libboost-dev in the apt lists of the setup script, its
  test and the CI workflows, and the Boost sentences of the docs and
  AGENTS.md.  The runtime headers changed, so the ABI stamp of every
  compiled module changed; make stage compiled the library again.
- The sqlite3 program.  configure checked for it as a prerequisite of
  icurry: cypm, the Curry Package Manager, keeps its package index in
  SQLite and needs the executable (its manual says so).  Nothing of
  Sprite runs it; the ICurry cache uses the sqlite3 module of the
  standard library (curry.cache, guarded by a try).  The check is gone;
  the installation steps of icurry note the need (the old step named the
  apt package sqlite, which does not exist; it is sqlite3).
- icurry is looked for only on request.  Before, a configure that found
  no front end looked for icurry as well and reported it missing, with
  the sqlite3 program behind it, although the icurry route needs the
  front end too (set_curry2icurry_tool aborts without it).  Now
  --with-icurry or ICURRY asks for it; otherwise it is not configured and
  not reported.  The prerequisite check in a clean environment on this
  machine (PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin, the project Python) went
  from "Missing: pakcs, pakcs-frontend, sqlite3, icurry.  Found 4
  problems." to "Missing: pakcs, pakcs-frontend.  Found 2 problems."; with
  the tools of Make.config it says "Found 0 problems." before and after.
