- The ABI stamp (open question 2), not changed, proposed.  object_digest
  digests the real path of the installation prefix (the repair of C6 of
  the audit of #82), so the shipped objects are stale under every
  environment prefix.  The condition of the lane for a change was "small,
  every existing test green": unit_cxx_toolchain.py TestFlavor.test_digest
  asserts that the digest changes with the prefix and equals a 16-digit
  hex string, so no relocatable form keeps that test as it is.  Proposal
  in conda/README.md: the stamp carries the real path of the installation
  as text beside the digest of the headers and the flags; conda-build then
  lists the stamps in info/has_prefix as text, conda rewrites them with the
  NEEDED entries, is_stale compares the text with the real path, a copy by
  hand stays stale, a relocated package keeps its objects (the measured
  gain: 1.66 s to 0.20 s on the first import, 31.7 s to 3.4 s on the first
  sprite-make --so, no write).
