- Review of the item (the same day), five findings.  (a) An object
  without its generated file (sprite-make --tidy removes the .cpp) whose
  import lost its object: the plan trusted the object and the loader
  raised DynloadError for the interpreted import.  Now
  Cpp2So.import_lacks_an_object reads the imports from the NEEDED entries
  of the object (loader.needed_modules) when the file is gone, so the
  importer is interpreted as with the file; the DynloadError stays for
  curry.load alone.  (b) The NEEDED entries followed the --as-needed
  default of the toolchain (g++ of Debian and Ubuntu pass it; conda
  compilers and other distributions do not): LINK_FLAGS pins
  -Wl,--no-as-needed, so the entries are the imports of the IMPORTS line
  in order on every toolchain, and the loader's pre-import covers every
  import of an object without its file.  The flag enters the digest, so
  make stage relinked the 13 library objects once more (43 s); every one
  names each of its imports now (Data.Function names sprite-Prelude.so.13,
  Control.Monad names libc.so.6).  (c) elf.read_dynamic read the dynamic
  section through the section headers and returned an empty result for
  an object without them; it finds the section through the program
  headers (PT_DYNAMIC) and the string table through the PT_LOAD that maps
  it, as the dynamic linker does, reads with seeks, and raises ValueError
  for a file without program headers or without a dynamic section (a
  relocatable object).  Checked against readelf on an installed object
  and on a copy after strip --strip-section-headers (binutils 2.42).  (d)
  An object-relative record counts on the layout of the toolchain; an
  object compiled elsewhere (a file of curry.save compiled in another
  directory, as TestRoundTrip does not) resolved it to a file that does
  not exist ("/M.curry" for /out/M.so).  loader.source_file now resolves
  such a record only for an object under a product directory
  (_filenames.curryfilename) and gives None otherwise, so the module has
  no source file rather than a wrong one; curry.save says where to
  compile the file.  (e) A docstring of 118 columns in the tests, wrapped.
