2026-10-08: the route on a cache hit, example 03 on the C++ backend, the hash rule and the note on the saved program (decisions 4 and 6 of the action list; worktree wt/potholes3)
- Decision 4, the route on a hit.  A hit of the ICurry cache wrote the
  .icy and the interfaces and left the .fcy of the front end as it was,
  so a pre-rewrite pair made again (make overlay over a tree whose cache
  held the module) disagreed until a hand rewrite (#101, left to the
  owner).  Now Curry2ICurryConverter.convert runs the binding
  optimization over the .fcy on a hit as well
  (_curry2icurry.rewrite_on_hit): a read; a parse when the text has an
  equality name (the exact test of "nothing to replace"; a rewritten
  file parses too, as after a miss, so the gap of a source that names
  constrEq itself is not widened); the file is written when the pass
