2026-10-08: Int is 64 bits with an error at the boundary, and the integer division by zero (#105, #106; worktree wt/apibugs)
- Diagnosis.  The Int of the C++ backend is int64_t, and the boundary was
  silent.  A Python int past the range reached the node through the Arg
  binding: the 64-bit overload of pybind11 refused it, the double overload
  took it, and the node held the bits of the nearest double (2**63 gave
  4890909195324358656).  plusInt, minusInt and timesInt wrapped (2**62 +
  2**62 gave the minimum).  truncate and round of a Float past the range
  cast an out-of-range double (1e30 gave the minimum).  quotInt and remInt
  divided through a double, so quot (2**53 + 1) 1 gave 2**53 and rem
  (2**53 + 1) 3 gave 3.  divInt and modInt divided by zero unchecked, and
  the process died with SIGFPE (exit 136); div minBound (-1) traps the
  same way.  The Python backend kept the Python integer and raised
  ZeroDivisionError.  The owner's default of 2026-10-08: 64 bits with an
  error at the boundary; the unbounded Int is a later item.
- Fix, C++ backend.  currylib/defs/checked.def is the template of a
  primitive on Int whose result may not exist: FUNC returns false, the
  step sets the error of the configuration (as prim_error does) and
  returns E_ERROR: catch takes it, and the scheduler raises it as
  EvaluationError.  math.cpp
  defines the nine checked primitives with the builtins of the compiler
  (__builtin_add_overflow and friends): plusInt, minusInt, timesInt;
  divInt, modInt, quotInt and remInt with the division by zero and the
  quotient of the minimum by -1 (the remainder of that pair is zero and
  is taken before the division, which traps on it); prim_truncateFloat
  and prim_roundFloat, which accept the integral doubles from -2^63 up to
  2^63 and refuse the rest, the infinities and NaN included.  quot and
  rem are integer divisions now, exact above 2**53.  The Arg binding
  (cyrtbindings/graph.cpp) gets an overload for a Python int that the
  64-bit overload refused; it raises CurryTypeError with the text of the
  Python backend.  The literals of the ICurry interpreter
  (cyrtbindings/icurry.cpp, an Int constant and the value set of a case)
  check the range with PyLong_AsLongAndOverflow and raise the same error;
  before, the cast of pybind11 raised a RuntimeError without the value
  and the module did not load.  No node layout changed.
- Fix, Python backend.  currylib/prelude/math.py has the twins: plusInt,
  minusInt, timesInt, the four divisions and the two conversions check the
  64-bit range and the zero divisor and raise EvaluationError with the
  same texts; quotInt is an integer division; prim_divFloat gives the IEEE
  result of a division by zero (an infinity, or NaN for 0.0 / 0.0) as the
  C++ backend does, instead of ZeroDivisionError.  prim_readNatLiteral
  of currylib/prelude/read.py fails the parse of a numeral outside the
  range, as the C++ step does on ERANGE (before this entry it returned
  the wide integer; after the range check of the node it raised the
  CurryTypeError inside the evaluation).  graph/node.py checks
  the range when an Int node is made, so the Python backend never holds a
  wider integer (one mask of the flags per node).  The generated Python
  binds the primitives when the file is written ("from _operator import
  sub as ..."), so compiler.FORMAT_VERSION is 7 and a file of format 6 is
  written again from its JSON; without the bump an installed Prelude.py
  kept the operators of Python (seen: a staged tree ran the old ones).
- The texts.  "integer overflow: 9223372036854775807 + 1", "integer
  overflow: (-9223372036854775808) * (-1)", "integer overflow: div
  (-9223372036854775808) (-1)", "integer overflow: truncate 1.0e+30",
  "integer overflow: round (-Infinity)", "division by zero: div 1 0".  A
  negative operand is in parentheses; a Float is spelled as show spells
  it.  negate x is 0 - x in the Prelude, so negate minBound names "0 -
  (-9223372036854775808)"; ceiling and floor convert through truncate and
  name it.  A Python int outside the range: "9223372036854775808 is
  outside the range of Int (-9223372036854775808 to 9223372036854775807)",
  a CurryTypeError on both backends through curry.expr, curry.raw_expr
  and curry.eval, at the node.
