2026-10-08: the ABI stamp digests the headers the generated code includes (issue #44, V4; worktree wt/v4)
- The set.  toolchain.runtime_headers returns the include closure of the
  headers the emitter writes into every generated file
  (compiler.RUNTIME_INCLUDES, today "cyrt/cyrt.hpp" alone; vEmitHeader
  writes one directive per name): the scan follows every quoted include
  recursively, resolved as the compiler resolves it (the directory of the
  including header first, then the include directory), a conditional
  include counted (trace.hpp under SPRITE_TRACE_ENABLED and
  state/counters.hpp under SPRITE_SCHEDULER_COUNTERS), the list sorted by
  the path relative to the include directory, so the digest does not
  depend on the order of the directives.  runtime_digest, object_digest
  and the precompiled header (PrecompiledHeader.header_files, which
  decides when a member is stale) take the set.  A header under
  include/cyrt that no include of the closure reaches is out of the
  digest: an edit to it rebuilds the runtime library (the .d files of
  src/Make.depends) and no module.  Kept: an installation without headers
  gives None (the root does not exist), a header that exists and cannot be
