2026-10-09: the shared capsule is cloned at its first divergence (decision D3
  of the memo on the Fair Scheme proofs, route (c); #86; worktree wt/capsule)
- The defect (the known failure test_shared_capsule, the owner's item of the
  entry of 2026-10-07).  A capsule started while a variable of its goal was
  free, consumed in part, and read again by two configurations that bound
  the variable differently after the start: the nested evaluation read the
  binding of the first reader through the queue stack (the fix of #97), put
  it into the nested spine, and consed the value onto the shared allValues
  node, which the other reader then took.  sharedCase and sharedEq gave
  (0, 1) twice where the plain goals give (0, 1) and (0, 2); sharedPat gave
  (0, 1) twice where the plain goal gives it once.
- The decision.  The owner approved the memo with its recommendations on
  2026-10-09: route (c), clone the capsule at the first divergence of the
  enclosing state, or index its nested state by that state; route (b), an
  ownership test with the narrowing route (a) for a shared capsule, as the
  fallback when (c) costs too much.  The bound for "too much", set before
  the measurements: a change of the steps or the forks of QueensSet, of
  QueensSet9 or of the shape of unit_funcpat_narrowed.py (a goal without a
  shared capsule pays nothing), or more than twice the steps of the private
  shapes (privateCase, privateEq) on the shared ones.  Route (c) is within
  the bound (below); route (b) was not needed.
- The rule, operationally.  A divergence is the first read, by the nested
  evaluation of a capsule, of a binding that the configuration which runs
  the capsule holds and the capsule does not.  The bindings are the one
  kind of enclosing state that enters a capsule without a choice node: a
  decision of a choice of the goal and a narrowing of a variable of it
  escape as choices and split the queue (the repair of #61), and a group
  made outside is restored at the escape.  get_binding (rts_freevars.cpp;
  _find_binding in rts_bindings.py) reports the level at which it found
  the binding: 0 for the map of the configuration or the bindings its
  queue absorbed (Queue::absorbed, new; Queue.absorbed), k for the k-th
  enclosing level.  A reader that puts a binding of a level above into the
  evaluation (replace_freevar, both overloads, and the walk of evalS_step;
  N, hnf, D and the walk on the Python backend) returns E_DIVERGE
  (RuntimeState::diverge; the exception E_DIVERGE), which every step hands
  out as it hands E_UNWIND out, up to the allValues_step of the
  configuration that holds the binding.  That step clones the queue
  (Queue::clone: the same configurations, shared and cloned before a step
  as after a split; the decisions; the absorbed bindings, plus the one
  read, under the id the configurations of the queue use), puts allValues
  of a new SetEval over the clone into a private copy of its spine, as a
  binding itself goes into an expression, and restarts.  The read then
  finds the binding at level 0.  The shared node stays for the other
  configurations, each of which clones the capsule at its own first read.
  Nested capsules diverge from the outside in: the outer queue is cloned
  for the reader, and at the next read the inner queue for the clone's
  configuration (sharedNested).  Two bindings cost two clones (sharedTwo).
  The clone is the index of route (c) made lazily: one nested state per
  enclosing state the capsule read.  The steps in between are left as
  they were, with their queues, as after E_UNWIND (procD sets
  forced_rotate); the collectors mark the absorbed bindings as roots.
- Three shortcuts keep the cost off goals without sharing.  The walk of
  evalS_step (private_state, which replaced holds_private_state) absorbs
  the bindings it meets into the new queue, so a capsule created after the
  binding never diverges on it.  A binding found at the outermost
  configuration while it is alone in its queue is absorbed in place, with
  no clone and no restart: no other configuration reaches the capsule, and
  a later clone of the configuration starts with the same binding (the
  reasoning of the shortcut of the walk).  Without it the last alternative
  alive, whose walk the shortcut skips, cloned the capsule at its first
  read and lost the sharing of the capsule between the two paths of
  twoValues (privateCase went from 110 to 137 steps on the C++ backend;
  back to 110 with it).  The outermost configuration alone in its queue
  takes no private copy, and it skips the walk when it holds no binding;
  when it holds one, the walk runs to absorb alone (the review below).
