2026-10-09: the checker of memo 6.5 (the run-time invariants of the Fair
  Scheme, first in the Python backend; worktree wt/checker)
- The task.  Section 6.5 of the memo on the Fair Scheme proofs asks for a
  checker mode, first in the Python backend, where instrumentation is cheap,
  then mirrored in the C++ runtime behind a flag (a later lane).  The owner
  approved the memo with its recommendations on 2026-10-09.  This entry
  delivers the Python checker: the flag, the checker object, its hooks, the
  checks of parts (1) to (5) of the lane, the tests, the cost, and the
  violations found.
- The flag.  ``checker`` (True | False, default False) in
  curry.interpreter.flags, documented with the other flags, in the flags
  table of the Python API page and in a section of the developer notes.
  The exact text for a run: SPRITE_INTERPRETER_FLAGS=backend:py,checker:true
  (the harness system py-check is the pair ('backend:py,checker:true', '')
  in the systems table of run.py).  The C++ backend accepts the flag and
  ignores it.
- The design.  RuntimeState.checker holds one Checker
  (backends/py/eval/checker.py) while the flag is on and None otherwise.
  Every hook in the runtime is one test of that attribute, so the flag-off
  path takes the same steps and makes the same nodes as before.  The
  checker observes: it never writes the state (it reads the union-find
  without path compression, the bindings without the absorption of
  _find_binding, and the generators without their creation).  A violation
  raises InvariantViolation, an AssertionError whose message names the
  invariant, the event, the detail, the identifiers, the configuration (its
  queue, its set, its index, escape_all, the fingerprint, the groups, the
  goal position from the call stack, the root expression) and, for a
  dispatch-chain disagreement, the enclosing configuration.
- The hooks (the four events the memo names, and the three the checks of
  FS-x and B2 need).  fork: rts_fingerprint.fork, after the clones are made
  (the generator collects them and calls the hook when the queue has taken
  them).  escape: rts_setfunctions.split_queue (rule SF.1), with the
  configurations of the queue before the split; update_escape_set, the
  insertion of an identifier by a pull-tab across a box.  pull-tab:
  rts_fingerprint.pull_tab, once before the rewrite with the two copies and
  once after it with the created choice.  yield: rts_control.release_value,
  before the value is made.  instantiation: rts_freevars.instantiate (rule
  S.x), before and after the write; rts_freevars._make_generator; the
  private copies of rule N.x in N (three sites) and hnf (the binding), and
  the value bindings of a builtin type in hnf.  step: fairscheme.S after a
  completed step, with the symbol and the successors the redex held before
  (the list object is kept, not copied: a step replaces it).  hnf: at the
  entry of fairscheme.hnf.  capsule entry: rts_setfunctions.create_queue.
  freshvar for the tags of a variable.
- The checks.  (2) B1: at every fork, escape and yield the fingerprint of
  each configuration involved is a function and its group invariant holds
  (every decided identifier agrees with the root of its group in the
  union-find of the configuration, and no member disagrees), and the
  fingerprints along the dispatch chain agree (def:s-chain of the note:
  the enclosing fingerprint is the union); each clone of a fork keeps
  every decision of its parent (read through the clone's groups), has the
  decision of the fork, in its own fingerprint or in an enclosing one, and
  adds at most the forked identifier and its group root (rule D.2; a fork
  on a free variable applies its bindings and equates its group, so the
  last clause is skipped for it); at most two clones with different
  sides.  A pull-tab gives the created choice the identifier of its
  source, the source is at the recorded path, the two alternatives are
  fresh copies of the spine that share the cells off the path and end in
  the alternative, and the identifier is in the escape set of every box
  the real path from the root to the source crosses (def:s-pull; the
  insertions precede the pull-tab in N and hnf, so the check is exact
  there, where the dropped-box defect below is found through the path
  alone).  At a yield no choice, operation,
  failure or constraint cell is reachable from the value; the generator of
  a free variable and the arguments of a partial application are not
  entered.  (3) FS-x.  X1: one generator per variable (the table of the
  checker), its root a choice with the variable's identifier, checked at
  the creation and at every instantiation.  X-c at a yield: no variable
  with a binding or a decision remains in the value, and for every
  variable of the table with a generator and a decided root the
  identifiers on the decided path of its generator are decided.  X-b' at
  an instantiation: the slot held the variable, the write put its
  generator there, and the reduct of every configuration of every queue
  that references the redex, read under the fingerprint it is compatible
  with, is the same before and after the write; after a copy of rule N.x
  the copy is a faithful copy of the spine with the replacement at its end
  and its reduct equals the reduct of the root it replaces.  The reduct is
  read with the generator image of the memo's revision: a decided choice
  is its side, a bound variable its binding or its generator, a free
  variable and an undecided generator root the group of the variable, and
  a forward node or a box is passed through; it is compared as a digest
  (blake2b over the cells), within a budget of 5000 cells per event; an
  event over the budget is counted (counts['over_budget']) and not
  compared.  None of the suite's goals reached the budget.  (4) FS-S.
  Every identifier is tagged at its creation with the boxes above it: the
  set guards crossed from the root of each configuration of the dispatch
  chain to the redex (the frames of the call stacks, as boxed_failure reads
  them, and escape_all), plus the flags of the redex cell.  The flags are
  the entry step of def:s-flags: at the creation of a capsule the cells
  reachable from its boxed arguments are flagged with the set (a bounded
  walk; a capsule beyond the budget turns its S0 checks off), and the
  cells a step, a pull-tab, a copy or a generator creates at a flagged
  cell inherit the flags (a bounded walk from the redex that stops at
  flagged cells).  A generator inherits the tags of its variable.  The
  tags define "argument-derived".  S0: an insertion into an escape set is
  of an argument-derived identifier (E in A); a fork inside a capsule is on
  an identifier that is function-derived for the capsule (its tags), that
  is in the escape set of no enclosing capsule (the shadow sets: the tags
  of an enclosing set over-approximate its escape set, since a choice a
  function makes inside the inner capsule is created under the box of the
  outer one; argAfterStart of SetFunctionsBugs is the case) and that no
  enclosing configuration decided, or on one the queue was split on
  before (the three clauses of def:s-escapes, as choice_escapes reads
  them);
  at SF.1 the escaping identifier is argument-derived for the capsule or an
  enclosing one of the chain, or an enclosing configuration decided it (the
  three clauses of def:s-escapes, read on the tags instead of the escape
  sets).  The escape sets only grow (a shadow per set; a loss and an
  insertion outside the rule are both reported).  S-split: after SF.1 the
  kept queue holds the LEFT and the undecided configurations, the new one
  the RIGHT and the undecided, nothing else and nothing lost, both record
  the identifier, both name one set.  (5) B2.  The definitional tree of an
  operation is rebuilt from the ICurry case structure of its body (the
  positions of the case variables through the IVarAccess assignments; a
  case on a variable that is not a position is left untracked), found
  through the symbol tables of the loaded modules by the info table of the
  redex.  At every hnf the position is a case of the tree of the operation
  at the redex whose branches above it match the constructors at their
  positions (B2 a, b).  After a step that replaced the redex by a failure
  the matched path ends in an exempt leaf, or in a literal case without a
  branch for the value (B2 c); a failure that hnf writes at an inductive
  position never reaches the hook (the step unwinds).  A built-in has no
  tree and is not checked; the Prelude functions with ICurry bodies are.
- The tests (tests/unit_py_checker.py, 38 tests; 35 skip on the C++
  backend).  TestKnownGood: the goals of the probe table under both failure
  rules, the goals of SetFunctionsBindings, the goals of
  unit_setfunctions_bugs.py, the functional-pattern modules, the goals of
  unit_cxx_freevars.py, and a module with the narrowed name of
  unit_funcpat_narrowed.py, a released residual, a narrowing and a pairing:
  each runs under the checker without a report and with the values it has
  without the flag (both runs in the test).  One constructed violation per
  check: the group invariant at a fork (a decided member of a group whose
  root is undecided), a clone that drops the fingerprint of its parent
  (Configuration.clone replaced in the test: without the check the goal
  dup2 gives 16 values for 4), the identifier and the copies of a
  pull-tab, a pull-tab across a box without the insertion into the escape
  set, a choice in a yielded value, a nested configuration against its enclosing one,
  a second generator and a wrong root identifier, a decided variable in a
  value, an undecided inner identifier, a copy whose reduct changed, an
  instantiation whose copy is corrupted off its path (copy_spine replaced
  in the test), an insertion of a function-derived identifier into an
  escape set, a fork inside a capsule on an argument-derived identifier, a
  fork inside a nested capsule on an identifier in the escape set of the
  enclosing set and one on an identifier the enclosing configuration
  decided (choice_escapes turned off for the state, since the runtime
  would split the queue), a split on a function-derived identifier, a split that keeps a decided
  configuration in both queues, an escape set that lost an element, a step
  that demands a position before the inductive position (the step function
  replaced in the test), a step that fails on a matched rule, and the flag
  itself.  TestDroppedBox pins the defect below (two known failures).
- The cost with the flag off.  The steps and the forks of the goals of
  unit_funcpat_narrowed.py are unchanged: one/source 107 steps 8 forks,
  many/source 12867 and 1202, distinct/source 1333 and 324, one/sourceS 122
  and 8, many/sourceS 12882 and 8, distinct/sourceS 1504 and 72,
  one/sourceN 111 and 8, many/sourceN 13468 and 1202, distinct/sourceN
  1594 and 450, before and after (and the same under the checker).  The
  wall time of Half.curry main on the Python backend (goal2, toPeano 1600):
  35.9, 35.2, 36.1 s before, 36.6, 36.4, 36.4 s after, on a shared machine:
  the mean rises 2 percent, at the edge of the spread of the runs; the
  flag-off path has one attribute test per step, per hnf, per pull-tab,
  per fork, per yield and per copy (fork allocates its list of clones
  under the test as well).  With the flag on the funcpat goals take 10.0 s
  for 4.8 s, and the checker holds memory as well as time: it keeps every
  flagged cell alive (the entry walk flags up to 50000 cells per capsule,
  a step or a copy up to 1024) for the life of the runtime state, so a
  long run of a capsule under the checker may need a larger address limit
  than the plain run (HARNESS_AS_LIMIT of the harness, 2 GiB by default).
- The runs.  The seven files of the lane under the checker through the
  runner (-j 2 --mem 4 --backend py, SPRITE_INTERPRETER_FLAGS=
  backend:py,checker:true): unit_funcpat_narrowed.py 2 of 2,
  unit_setfunctions_semantics.py 41 of 41 (both failure rules through its
  children, which inherit the flag), unit_cxx_freevars.py 7 of 7 (its
  Python half), unit_setfunctions_bindings.py 16 of 16,
  unit_py_residuation.py 6 of 6, unit_funpat_free_argument.py 9 of 9, and
  unit_setfunctions_bugs.py 21 of 22: test_captured_then_guarded reports
  the defect below; 34 s wall.  With the flag off the unit_py_* files, the
  seven files and the new file: 21 of 21 files, 0 failed, 39 s wall.  The
  new file on the C++ backend: 34 tests, 31 skipped, ok.  make -C docs
  html: build succeeded.
- The violations found.  (1) A true defect of the Python backend, found at
  the pull-tab check (B1: the source is not at the recorded path): in the
  walk of N a forward node at the cursor is replaced by
  indexing.logical_subexpr(parent, index, update_fwd_nodes=True), which
  skips the forward chain and the set guards behind it, while the real
  path of the walk and its list of set ids stay as they were.  A choice
  behind a box behind a forward node is then pull-tabbed along a path that
  omits the box: the copies of the spine lose the guard, and the escape
  set of the capsule is not updated.  A captured choice reached through a
  forward node alone is encapsulated.  Reproducer (data T = A | B;
  constT t _ = t; pickOne z f = [z] ? [f 0]; oneCaptured = let x = A ? B in
  let vs = sortValues (set2 pickOne A (constT x)) in (length vs, x)): the
  Python backend gives (3, A) and (3, B), the C++ backend (2, A) and
  (2, B), the values of weakly encapsulated search.  The goal
  capturedThenGuarded of unit_setfunctions_bugs.py has the same walk and
  passes by the second, boxed occurrence of the choice, which escapes and
  sorts the configurations forked too early.  The fix is in the T_FWD case
  of N (fairscheme.py): step through the forward chain and the guards one
  node at a time, with the real path and the set ids extended as the walk
  does for a guard at the cursor; not made in this lane.  Pinned in
  TestDroppedBox (test_values, a known failure on the Python backend;
  test_under_the_checker, a known failure; test_report, the message).  (2)
  A false alarm, fixed in the checker: the first form of the fork check
  required the clone's own fingerprint to hold the decision; a nested fork
  on an identifier an enclosing configuration decided writes nothing
  (update_fp reads the decision through the queue stack and keeps one
  side).  The check reads the decision through the chain.  No other report
  on the goals of the lane.
- The review of the lane (2026-10-09, seven findings) and what was done.
  (1) The fork check did not relate the clone to its parent (rule D.2):
  confirmed with Configuration.clone replaced to give an empty
  fingerprint, dup2 then gives 16 values with no report; the check
  _check_clone above was added, with the test.  (2) sprite-exec prints an
  InvariantViolation, an AssertionError, as "an internal error occurred.
  Rerun with SPRITE_DEBUG=1 for details." (ProgramErrorHandler.print_error
  of curry.tools.utility): confirmed on the reproducer, with and without
  SPRITE_DEBUG=1.  The output of sprite-exec is the owner's; the report of
  a violation needs SPRITE_DEBUG=1 under sprite-exec today, and the
  developer notes say so.  (3) B2 is asserted for the operations with an
  ICurry body alone: on the set-function and functional-pattern goals of
  the suite 10773 of 16492 hnf calls are untracked built-ins (plusInt
  4947, nonstrictEq 1555, apply 771, cond 583, eqChar 552, allValues 442,
  _biString 397, & 397, constrEq 390, ltEqInt 140, evalS 122, applyS 118,
  set 104, $! 84, eqInt 82 lead); stated in the notes and here; no
  hand-written tree table for the strict built-ins was added.  (4) The S0
  fork check read the tags of the current set alone: the three clauses of
  def:s-escapes are checked now (see the checks above).  A first form that
  read the tags of the enclosing sets reported argAfterStart, a false
  alarm: the tags over-approximate the escape sets of the enclosing sets.
  (5) The yield walk does not enter the arguments of a partial application
  (pa = (+) (1 ? 2) yields a function value with the choice inside it, no
  report), nor the generator of a free variable: stated in the notes and
  here as a reading the paper must carry; whether the model's value
  definition treats a partial application as data is the owner's
  question.  (6) fork allocated its list of clones with the flag off:
  guarded now; the notes say "one attribute test per event" and name the
  memory the checker holds.  The steps and the forks of the funcpat goals
  are the same as before, flag off and on.  (7) The pull-tab check did not
  assert the insertions of def:s-pull: added (_check_crossed_boxes), with
  the test.  After the changes: unit_py_checker.py 38 tests ok (2 expected
  failures) on the Python backend and ok (35 skipped) on the C++ backend;
  the seven files under the checker through the runner: 7 of 7 run, 1
  failed (test_captured_then_guarded, the dropped-box defect), 32 s wall.
- Left to the owner.  (1) The C++ mirror of the checker behind the same
  flag.  (2) The defect of (1) above: the fix in N, an issue, and the
  values of oneCaptured as a test of both backends.  (3) Not checked: the
  lifts of the constraints of =:= and =:<= (FS-beta, E-lift; the memo's
