  backend has one schedule; the harness compares the rotation modes of the
  C++ backend), the private copies of the spine that a set function makes
  for a configuration (evalS and the clone of a capsule), and the
  one-constructor case of X-c (such a variable has no root identifier to
  decide).  (4) Two approximations to state in the paper or to tighten:
  "argument-derived" is read from the tags (the boxes above the creation
  site, the entry flags and their inheritance), not from per-cell flags of
  every cell, and the cells a step creates are flagged by a walk from the
  redex that stops at flagged cells; the reduct comparison of X-b' is a
  digest within a budget, so a goal whose configurations exceed 5000 cells
  per instantiation is counted, not compared (none of the suite's goals
  did).  (5) tests/manifest.json has no entry for unit_py_checker.py (a
  calibration run adds it).  (6) The deferred nested-guard assertion of
